    basic: "In Phase 1, use your 7s to throw away junk cards and win tricks with your Aces to draw fresh cards from the Talon. Don't waste high cards until the Talon is nearly empty.",
    intermediate: "Count the 10s. Since 10s are worth 10 points but rank below Aces, they are easy to lose if you lead them too early. Try to 'duck' tricks that contain 10s unless you are sure you can win.",
    advanced: "Phase 2 Preparation: Watch which cards your partner is 'throwing' during Phase 1. If they throw a 7 of Hearts, it's a signal to play Hearts in Phase 2 because they are likely void or holding trumps to protect that suit.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'If you have a Trump Marriage (K+O), declare it immediately on your lead. 40 points is nearly 40% of the way to victory.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Know when to stop the game. If you've been tracking tricks and know you are at 101, call 'Out!' before your opponent can catch up.",
      },
